  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.2,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.08,
    "rationale": "The sudden plateau at about 1.15 after exponential growth could have meant the reader was saturating. To test this, I diluted retained late aliquots into the reader's linear range. At 18 h, a 10x dilution read 0.1185 and 0.1217 (×10 gives 1.19–1.22), and a 20x dilution read 0.0614 (×20 gives 1.23). At 14 h, a 10x dilution read 0.1182 (×10 gives 1.18), compared with an undiluted reading of 1.10. The corrected values from both dilutions agree with each other and with the undiluted readings (about 1.16–1.19) to within about 3–6%. The 20x value is slightly higher, which could be mild nonlinearity, but the difference is far too small to point to a hidden higher biomass. If the reader were saturated, the dilutions would have given much higher corrected values. So the late plateau is real, probably stationary phase, at about OD 1.2."
  },
